{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PS2 assessment of the 7-day failure-mining signals against change 1791:\n\nRISK 1 (mixed-evidence false positives) — CONFIRMED and fixed. Empirical check on the PS1 guard: (a) a tagged AC whose provenance declares external evidence but whose prose names a repo path for ORIENTATION (\"the fix shipped in src/rebar/_store/sync.py is deployed to prod\") falsely fired. (b) A genuinely MIXED criterion (test file cited as the repo-verifiable half + external exit-code outcome) fired — that one is intended policy: SPLIT.\n\nPS2 detector change (det_attestation_launder.py): citations are now judged per-line with an evidence-vs-orientation rule. Test-shaped citations (tests/ paths, test_* segments/symbols, pytest ::node ids) ALWAYS fire — a test is inherently completion proof, never orientation. Other repo citations (src/, docs/, code-extension slash paths) fire only when an evidence-introducing word (proxy/proof/evidence/verified/covered/documented/...) precedes them on the same line. URLs scrubbed first; commit SHAs / Gerrit numbers still never fire (ADR-0043 provenance). The block message now explicitly coaches the SPLIT for mixed criteria: cited paths/symbols move to a new UNTAGGED criterion; the external outcome keeps the tag with its provenance line.\n\nRISK 2 (f680 catch-22) — evaluated, exemption NOT implemented, deliberately. Normalizing [operator-attested] tag edits out of the plan-review material fingerprint is not a small contained change (it touches the signed-hash contract), and a direction-insensitive exemption would let post-certification RETAGGING escape attestation invalidation — the exact laundering vector this bug closes (fb8a's re-review only happened BECAUSE the retag staled the attestation). Mitigation shipped instead: both block messages now state that the untag/split/provenance edit stales the signed plan-review attestation and to expect re-running rebar review-plan, so the re-review cycle is documented, not a surprise. Follow-up recommendation: if a DIRECTION-SENSITIVE seam is ever designed (tag-REMOVE + provenance-line-ADD exempt; tag-ADD always material), that could safely cut the two extra review cycles — file it as its own ticket with a signing-contract review.\n\nPS2 validation: 9 new tests (orientation no-fire, mixed fires + split coaching, marker-position pin, cross-line dedupe, URL-scrub-at-laundering-level, bare-test-symbol, staleness message x2); 8/8 new-logic mutants killed (incl. one survivor N8 — URL scrub in the per-line path — killed by a new test); make lint + typecheck + complexity ratchet clean; targeted suites 56 passed; broad unit suite 2157 passed (only known-environmental failures)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786744376072016001,"uuid":"31fc9190-b903-485e-88de-fca425f08f70"}